    {
      "bbox": [
        201,
        941,
        1905,
        1401
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The present administration of New York City has established as major goals the achievement of better housing for all segments of the City's populations; the creation of expanded job opportunities through the establishment of industrial parks and facilities; and the improvement and expansion of parks and recreational facilities so as to afford suitable environmental conditions for all who live and work in our City.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.2539,
          "min": -1.5958
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 68,
          "mean": -0.006,
          "min": -0.2264
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 0,
        "area_px": 750750,
        "density": 0.0,
        "chars": 417,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": null
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        201,
        1438,
        1954,
        2472
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Much has been accomplished towards the attainment of these goals. Urban renewal and low- and middle-income housing programs have been instituted and are being carried out on a scale that far surpass any other city in the nation; housing rehabilitation programs designed to save neighborhoods and preserve the existing housing stock have been instituted and are in progress; building code inspection and enforcement activities have been greatly expanded and intensified; a program for the development of urban industrial parks is being implemented; a massive program of land acquisition for parks, waterfront and other recreational activities is underway; and one of the most human and efficient relocation programs of contemporary times is in progress. New agencies, such as the Housing and Redevelopment Board, the Department of Relocation, the Rent and Rehabilitation Administration and a Department of Commerce and Industrial Development, were needed and created in order to initiate the progress of these programs.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2361,
          "min": -1.791
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 169,
          "mean": -0.0086,
          "min": -0.5767
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 0,
        "area_px": 1737612,
        "density": 0.0,
        "chars": 1018,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": null
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        201,
        2502,
        1942,
        2971
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "To provide coordination in the planning and execution of the program carried out by the various agencies concerned, a Housing Policy Board and a Housing Executive Committee were established. To provide tighter coordination, greater integration of planning, more centralized budget review, and greater precision in timing of projects and activities, supervision of these programs by a single executive responsible to the Mayor is desirable.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2575,
          "min": -1.7495
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 71,
          "mean": -0.0011,
          "min": -0.0328
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 0,
        "area_px": 784464,
